 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to information that\nresidential health care facilities are required to provide to residents and\ntheir families",
    "basePrintNo": "S9555",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9555-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2803, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9555\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to information that\nresidential health care facilities are required to provide to residents\nand their families\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill expands the information that must be made available to resi-\ndents and their families in a separate document as a part of an intake\napplication.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends subdivision 13 of section 2803 of the public health\nlaw by adding paragraph 13-a, requiring residential health care facili-\nties to include - in the document they have to provide to residents and\ntheir families - an explanation of the ownership structure of the facil-\nity, including the current board of directors and/or members of any\nlimited liability entity, and any contractors involved with major func-\ntions of the facility, including staffing, food, and linen service.\n\nSection two provides for the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill aims at expanding the information which must be made available\nto prospective residents and their families about residential health\ncare facilities. The information would include details regarding the\nownership structure of the facility, including the current board of\ndirectors and/or members of any limited liability entity, and any\ncontractors involved with major functions of the facility, such as\nstaffing, food, and linen service.\n\nBy expanding the current information, transparency and accountability\nare increased. Furthermore, it allows consumers and advocates to have a\nclearer understanding of who they are able to address with concerns.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:.\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
